repani.com -- the site as one archive. Render a page:
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page index -o index.html
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page fleet-engineer -o fleet-engineer/index.html
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page decision-desk -o decision-desk/index.html
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page privacy -o legal/privacy.html
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page terms -o legal/terms.html
    pica html -txtar site.txtar -page company -o legal/company.html
Members: page.tmpl (html/template shell), index.t.tmpl,
fleet-engineer.t.tmpl, decision-desk.t.tmpl, privacy.t.tmpl, terms.t.tmpl and company.t.tmpl (pica documents
as text/templates over the facts), data.fact (the site's facts, stated once), logo.svg (the mark and the name).
-- page.tmpl --
{{- /* Site links are relative ($up is the way back to the site root),
       so a page works at / and under /draft/ alike. */ -}}
{{- $up := "./"}}{{if ne .Page "index"}}{{$up = "../"}}{{end -}}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{if eq .Page "index"}}{{.Facts.site.title}}. {{.Title}}{{else}}{{.Title}} | {{.Facts.site.title}}{{end}}</title>
{{- if eq .Page "index"}}
<!-- Load-bearing: these two tags make `go get repani.com/...` resolve.
     The module root is the repo root; every path under it (ascon, golay,
     lz4s, pica, fact) resolves through this one page because longer URLs
     404 here. Never remove or reword them. -->
<meta name="go-import" content="repani.com git https://github.com/repani-ltd/repani">
<meta name="go-source" content="repani.com https://github.com/repani-ltd/repani https://github.com/repani-ltd/repani/tree/main{/dir} https://github.com/repani-ltd/repani/blob/main{/dir}/{file}#L{line}">
{{- end}}
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="description" content="{{.Facts.site.subhead}} {{.Facts.company.statement}}">
<link rel="icon" href="{{$up}}favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
<link rel="icon" href="{{$up}}favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{$up}}apple-touch-icon.png">
<style>
  @font-face { font-family: "Repani Mono"; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url("{{$up}}fonts/repani-mono-regular.woff2") format("woff2"); }
  @font-face { font-family: "Repani Mono"; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; src: url("{{$up}}fonts/repani-mono-bold.woff2") format("woff2"); }
  @font-face { font-family: "Repani Text"; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url("{{$up}}fonts/repani-text-regular.woff2") format("woff2"); }
  :root { --paper: #FEFAE0; --ink: #2B2D42; --muted: #5F6778; --red: #C1121F; --rule: #E3DFC8;
          --mono: "Repani Mono", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
          --text: "Repani Text", Georgia, serif; }
  html { background: var(--paper); -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
  body { box-sizing: border-box; max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 2.5rem; color: var(--ink);
         font-family: var(--text); font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.55; font-synthesis: none; }
  header { margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  header a { display: inline-block; }
  header svg { display: block; height: 2.6rem; width: auto; }
  a { color: var(--red); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  h1, h2, h3, table, dt, p.link, body > footer { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-ligatures: none; }
  article { counter-reset: section; }
  article h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  article h2 { counter-increment: section; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.4; margin: 3.75rem 0 1rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  article h2::before { content: counter(section) "."; display: inline-block; min-width: 2.2em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }
  article h3 { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 4.4vw, 1.6rem); line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  article h3 + h3 { margin-top: -.85rem; }
  article p { margin: 0 0 1em; }
  article p.byline { color: var(--muted); }
  article p.link { font-size: .9rem; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  article p.link::before { content: "\2192\00a0"; color: var(--muted); }
  article ul { padding-left: 1.2em; margin: 0 0 1em; }
  article dl { margin: 0 0 1em; }
  article dt { font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 700; }
  article dd { margin: 0 0 .9em; }
  article table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  article th, article td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: .55em 1em .55em 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  article th { font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  article td:last-child, article th:last-child { padding-right: 0; }
  article td:first-child { color: var(--muted); }
  body.home header { margin-bottom: 4.5rem; }
  body.home article h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5.9vw, 2.55rem); margin-bottom: .35em; }
  body.home article h1 + p { font-family: var(--mono); font-variant-ligatures: none; font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3vw, 1.4rem); line-height: 1.3; margin-bottom: 1.75rem; }
  body.home article h1 + p + p { font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  body > footer { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: .8rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); color: var(--muted); font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  body > footer a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .15em; }
  body > footer a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
</head>

<body{{if eq .Page "index"}} class="home"{{end}}>
<header>
  <a href="{{$up}}" aria-label="{{.Facts.site.title}}">{{.Raw.logo}}</a>
</header>
{{.Article}}
<footer>&copy; {{.Facts.company.copyright_year}} {{.Facts.company.name}} &middot; <a href="{{$up}}fleet-engineer/">Fleet Engineer</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}decision-desk/">Decision Desk</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}legal/privacy.html">Privacy</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}legal/terms.html">Terms</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}legal/company.html">Company</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}AGENTS.md">Agents</a> &middot; <a href="{{$up}}site.txtar">Source</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
-- index.t.tmpl --
{{.site.headline}}
.rem Root page. Rendered by: pica html -txtar site.txtar -page index -o index.html

{{.site.subhead}}

{{.company.statement}}

# Zero Handoff.

## Everyone is a Fleet Engineer. Nobody waits.

{{.site.zero_handoff}}

A software project is a chain of handoffs. Take away the handoffs and the
project is gone.

Fleet Engineers work in parallel. No one is blocked waiting for an analyst,
a backend or frontend developer, or QA. Expertise differs; the role does not.

# The thesis

## Don't add agents to the team. Rebuild the team around the agents.

A live project at a tier-1 global bank, in the middle of normal agile delivery,
threw out the way software teams have worked for decades.

Agents added to the old team would never have done it. So the team itself was
rebuilt. Everyone a Fleet Engineer, working in parallel, where a chain of
specialists used to wait on each other.

{{.reference.result}}

When factories first got electricity, most swapped the steam engine for a motor
and kept the layout. Productivity barely moved for decades. The gains came when
the floor was redesigned around the new power.

Paul A. David, "The Dynamo and the Computer", American Economic Review, 1990.

.table 18L 22L *L
^ | The usual team | The rebuilt team
Who does the work | A chain of specialists | Agents, directed by Fleet Engineers
Who answers for it | Divided along the chain | The Fleet Engineer who signs
Human roles | Analyst, backend developer, frontend developer, QA | One: Fleet Engineer
Who waits for whom | Specialists wait on each other | Nobody waits
.end

# Fleet Engineer

## Fewer engineers. Far better ones.

The Fleet Engineer is what is left when the team has been rebuilt.

{{.site.fleet_engineer}}

{{.site.fleet_engineer_skill}}
.link fleet-engineer/ The definition

# Accountability

## An agent can do the work. It can't answer for it.

## That's why you're here.

We know what a tier-1 bank demands before anything goes live. The controls stay.
The waiting goes.

# The Decision Desk

## {{.site.decision_desk_judgment}}

{{.site.decision_desk_shift}}

{{.site.decision_desk}} It approves what the agents have done, decides the cases
that are not routine, says no when the machine is wrong, and answers for the
result.

{{.site.decision_desk_people}}
.link decision-desk/ The definition

# The reference

.table 18L *L
^ | Tier-1 global bank
Platform | Of global importance
Delivery | By agents
Human roles on the team | One, in place of the usual split of specialists
Vetting | Every line, by a human
Result | {{.reference.result}}
.end

Zero Handoff was the way of working.

The public code was built with agents. An engineer can read it.
.link {{.go.repo}} Public code

# The company

{{.company.name}} is a company registered in {{.company.jurisdiction}}. It is
itself operated by agents, including the maintenance of this site.
.link legal/company.html Company details

.width 64
-- fleet-engineer.t.tmpl --
Fleet Engineer
.rem Rendered by: pica html -txtar site.txtar -page fleet-engineer -o fleet-engineer/index.html

{{.site.fleet_engineer}}

Repani's use of the term is defined here.

# The role

.term End to end
A Fleet Engineer takes a piece of work from the first conversation to
production.
.term In parallel
Fleet Engineers work in parallel, each with a fleet of agents. Nobody waits for
anybody.
.term Vets
A Fleet Engineer vets what the agents produce.
.term Signs
The Fleet Engineer signs for it. The signature is a person's, not an agent's.

# What it replaces

A chain of specialists waiting on each other: an analyst, a backend or frontend
developer, QA. Expertise differs; the role does not.

{{.site.fleet_engineer_skill}}

# What it is not

Not server infrastructure. The fleet is a fleet of agents, not of machines.

Not one person doing everything alone. Fleet Engineers work alongside others
doing the same.

# Where it comes from

The Fleet Engineer is what is left when the team has been rebuilt around the
agents. The way of working is called Zero Handoff. {{.site.zero_handoff}}
.link ../ Zero Handoff

# Citing this page

{{.company.name}}, "Fleet Engineer", {{.company.site}}/fleet-engineer/

.width 64
-- decision-desk.t.tmpl --
Decision Desk
.rem Rendered by: pica html -txtar site.txtar -page decision-desk -o decision-desk/index.html

{{.site.decision_desk}}

Repani's use of the term is defined here.

# What changes

## {{.site.decision_desk_judgment}}

{{.site.decision_desk_shift}}

# What the desk does

.term Decides
The desk decides the cases that are not routine.
.term Approves
It approves what the agents have done.
.term Says no
It says no when the machine is wrong.
.term Notices
It notices what looks off, because its people have seen it before.
.term Teaches
It teaches the agents how things are really done.
.term Answers
It answers for the result.

# The people

{{.site.decision_desk_people}}

# Citing this page

{{.company.name}}, "Decision Desk", {{.company.site}}/decision-desk/

.width 64
-- privacy.t.tmpl --
Privacy
.rem Rendered by: pica html -txtar site.txtar -page privacy -o legal/privacy.html

This site is a set of static pages. It sets no cookies, runs no
scripts, embeds no third-party content and contains no forms; it
collects no personal data and performs no analytics or tracking.

The pages are served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub
receives the technical data a browser sends with each request (such
as IP address, user agent and the page requested) and handles it
under the GitHub General Privacy Statement. {{.company.name}} does not
receive, store or process that data.
.link https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement GitHub General Privacy Statement

If you write to us, we keep your message for as long as the
correspondence needs; we do not share it and do not add you to any
list.

.width 64
-- terms.t.tmpl --
Terms of use
.rem Rendered by: pica html -txtar site.txtar -page terms -o legal/terms.html

The content of this site is provided for information, as is,
without warranty of any kind. {{.company.name}} accepts no liability
for its use or for the content of sites it links to.

Software published by {{.company.name}} is licensed under the terms
stated in each repository; those terms, not this page, govern its
use.

Text and the Repani mark on this site are © {{.company.name}}.
The mark may be shown unaltered to refer to {{.company.name}} or its
projects and may not be used to suggest endorsement.

.width 64
